1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,457
A reward headline is only the start

2
00:00:02,457 --> 00:00:03,510
of the story.

3
00:00:03,510 --> 00:00:05,265
Is the work still open?

4
00:00:05,265 --> 00:00:06,669
Is the sponsor verifiable?

5
00:00:06,669 --> 00:00:08,775
Can the payout actually reach you?

6
00:00:08,775 --> 00:00:11,232
RewardRadar is built to help answer one

7
00:00:11,232 --> 00:00:13,689
practical question before you commit your next

8
00:00:13,689 --> 00:00:14,040
hour.

9
00:00:14,260 --> 00:00:17,338
Here, the user asks whether any available

10
00:00:17,338 --> 00:00:19,097
work is worth pursuing.

11
00:00:19,097 --> 00:00:22,176
This is a voice-client simulation: the visual

12
00:00:22,176 --> 00:00:25,254
interface turns that request into a real

13
00:00:25,254 --> 00:00:28,332
tool call to RewardRadar's local Model Context

14
00:00:28,332 --> 00:00:29,212
Protocol server.

15
00:00:29,432 --> 00:00:32,669
The client negotiates MCP twenty twenty-five dash

16
00:00:32,669 --> 00:00:35,907
eleven dash twenty-five, discovers the available tools,

17
00:00:35,907 --> 00:00:37,757
and requests a search.

18
00:00:37,757 --> 00:00:40,994
The server ranks its timestamped demonstration records

19
00:00:40,994 --> 00:00:44,232
and returns structured results with the source,

20
00:00:44,232 --> 00:00:46,544
assumptions, and a planning verdict.

21
00:00:46,764 --> 00:00:50,015
Now we inspect funding instead of trusting

22
00:00:50,015 --> 00:00:50,944
the headline.

23
00:00:50,944 --> 00:00:54,196
Escrow, sponsor verification, acceptance criteria, and payout

24
00:00:54,196 --> 00:00:56,053
setup are separate signals.

25
00:00:56,053 --> 00:00:57,911
Missing evidence remains visible.

26
00:00:57,911 --> 00:01:01,163
A listed reward is never described as

27
00:01:01,163 --> 00:01:02,556
money already earned.

28
00:01:02,776 --> 00:01:05,338
RewardRadar checks the submission record, too.

29
00:01:05,338 --> 00:01:07,901
The Alexa-plus Devpost entry is submitted.

30
00:01:07,901 --> 00:01:10,890
No award has been announced, and no

31
00:01:10,890 --> 00:01:12,598
payment has been received.

32
00:01:12,598 --> 00:01:15,588
Those are three different states, and the

33
00:01:15,588 --> 00:01:17,296
interface keeps them distinct.

34
00:01:17,516 --> 00:01:20,284
This prototype runs locally on a checked-in

35
00:01:20,284 --> 00:01:20,680
fixture.

36
00:01:20,680 --> 00:01:23,448
It is not connected to an Alexa

37
00:01:23,448 --> 00:01:26,216
device or a live rewards feed, and

38
00:01:26,216 --> 00:01:28,589
its planning estimates are not guarantees.

39
00:01:28,589 --> 00:01:31,357
RewardRadar makes the evidence easier to hear—and

40
00:01:31,357 --> 00:01:34,125
easier to inspect—before you decide what to

41
00:01:34,125 --> 00:01:34,916
do next.
